Brand assets
------------

  The Huntloop mark — the loop that spirals in and closes on its target
    packages/ui/src/brand.ts            (geometry)
    packages/ui/src/components/BrandMark.tsx
    apps/web/app/icon.svg, apps/web/app/apple-icon.tsx,
    apps/web/app/opengraph-image.tsx    (renderings of the same geometry)

  Created and designed by Chandra Mani Sharma — the product thinking,
  design, architecture and connecting of the overall Huntloop system.
  Original work, drawn from first principles as an Archimedean spiral and
  a centred dot — not derived from a template, stock library or
  generative tool.

  Retired, not shipped:
    HuntLoop_SVGs/*.svg

  These are the earlier ribbon marks, which also shipped as PNGs under
  apps/web/public/brand/ until the mark above replaced them. Their
  provenance was never recorded — if they are ever brought back, whoever
  knows who made them and on what terms should record it here first.

  The name "Huntloop" is used as a trademark. No registration is recorded
  here. Whether one is needed, and in which classes and territories, is a
  question for counsel.


Design influences
-----------------

Not licensing matters, recorded because the design system's own comments name
them and a reader should be able to tell influence from reuse:

  · The dark palette and chrome derive from Supabase's visual language
    (near-black layered surfaces, a single saturated green accent, hairline
    borders, no shadows). No Supabase code or asset is used — the tokens in
    `packages/ui/src/tokens.css` are written from scratch and every contrast
    ratio in them was measured independently.
  · The dashboard information architecture derives from Kima BD OS.
  · The light palette derives from reference report screenshots.


Software dependencies
---------------------

479 packages resolve into `node_modules`. The distribution is overwhelmingly
permissive: 391 MIT, 38 Apache-2.0, 15 ISC, 17 BSD-2/3-Clause, with the
remainder BlueOak-1.0.0, MIT-0, CC0-1.0, 0BSD, Python-2.0 and Unlicense.

**No copyleft or source-available licence reaches the browser bundle.** Each
of the non-permissive ones below was checked individually and is build-time
or development-time only:

  @sentry/cli, @sentry/cli-win32-x64   FSL-1.1-MIT
      Functional Source License: source-available with a non-compete clause,
      converting to MIT two years after each release. Used only to upload
      source maps during a build. Huntloop does not compete with Sentry, so
      the clause is not engaged — but this is the one licence here that is
      not simply permissive, and it is recorded rather than assumed.

  @img/sharp-win32-x64                 Apache-2.0 AND LGPL-3.0-or-later
      The LGPL portion is the bundled libvips, dynamically linked, used for
      build-time image optimisation. Not redistributed by the application.

  axe-core, lightningcss                MPL-2.0
      File-level copyleft. Neither is modified. `axe-core` arrives only as a
      transitive dependency of eslint-plugin-jsx-a11y and is also used
      directly by the accessibility test in `e2e/a11y.spec.ts`.

  caniuse-lite                          CC-BY-4.0
      Browser-support data, consumed at build time. Attribution: the
      caniuse.com database, by Alexis Deveria and contributors.

Run `npm ls --all` for the complete resolved tree. This summary was generated
by walking every `package.json` under `node_modules` and is accurate as of
the audit dated 21 September 2026.
